Title:
Structured Hierarchy for Objectives, Strategies, KPIs, and AI-driven Execution

User Story Description:

As a Marketing Planner using Grower,
I want a clear, step-by-step structured workflow that allows me to define marketing objectives and measurable goals, associate detailed strategies to achieve these objectives, and set clear KPIs. Once defined, I want Grower’s built-in AI engine to automatically suggest organized Groups and detailed Initiatives, ensuring a clear hierarchy and smooth alignment from strategy down to execution.

This structured approach ensures effective alignment between high-level business objectives and tactical marketing execution, resulting in optimized marketing performance and clear operational clarity.

High-Level Hierarchy Logic (Grower Workflow)

The marketing planning hierarchy in Grower follows this structured logic:

Objectives & Goals

High-level strategic direction defining "what" you aim to achieve.

Clearly measurable Goals for evaluating success.

Strategies

Clearly defined action plans outlining "how" Objectives and Goals will be achieved.

Must directly link to Objectives and detail budget, timelines, audience personas, and channels.

KPIs (Key Performance Indicators)

Specific quantifiable metrics tracking the effectiveness and progress of Strategies.

AI-Generated Groups & Initiatives

Automated tactical suggestions aligning directly with Strategies and Goals, ensuring actionable execution at the operational level.

