User Story 1: Configure Group Objective Category, Associate with Strategies, and Map Metrics (From Group View/Edit)

Title: Configure Group Objective Category, Associate with Strategies, and Map Metrics (From Group View/Edit)

User Story:

As a Marketing Planner using Grower,
When viewing or editing an existing Group, I want to confirm or set its single "Objective Category" (formerly Primary Objective; Secondary Objective is deprecated), understand that the displayed 'Top Metrics' are category indicators, associate the Group with one or more relevant Strategies (based on matching Objective Category and timeline compatibility), and precisely map its campaign metrics to the Strategies' Key Results,
so that I can classify the Group correctly, establish clear strategic linkage, and enable accurate KR tracking based on specific mapped metrics, not the default Top Metrics.

Context Note on Deprecated Fields & Group Metrics:

The field previously known as "Secondary Objective" for Groups has been removed from the UI and creation process.

The field previously known as "Primary Objective" is now functionally the "Objective Category," acting as the primary classification and linking mechanism.

The "Top Metrics To Track" displayed on the Group page (based on the selected Objective Category) are default indicators for common performance related to that category. They are NOT automatically used for KR progress calculation. KR progress is determined only by the metrics explicitly mapped during the Group-to-Strategy association process outlined below.

Complete Logic & Workflow:

Pre-requisites:

User is viewing or editing an existing Group. Existing groups will have their former "Primary Objective" value automatically treated as their "Objective Category". New groups require selecting an "Objective Category".

Relevant Strategies exist with a defined "Objective Category", associated KRs, and defined Start/End Dates.

User has appropriate permissions (e.g., Edit Group).

Step 1: Confirm/Set Objective Category

Within the Group view/edit interface, the "Objective Category" is clearly displayed and editable (if permissions allow).

A tooltip explains: "Select the category that best classifies this Group's focus. This links the Group to relevant Strategies and Key Results."

Step 2: Initiate Strategy Association

User clicks a dedicated UI element like "Associate Strategies", "Manage Strategy Associations", or similar.

Step 3: Select Strategies for Association

A modal or dedicated UI section appears.

UI Title: "Associate Group '[Group Name]' with Strategies"

Displays a list of Strategies filtered to show only those sharing the same Objective Category as the current Group.

Information shown per Strategy: Strategy Name, Strategy Start Date, Strategy End Date, List/Count of KRs targeted.

Timeline Validation (Pre-selection Check): For each Strategy listed:

No Overlap: The Strategy is greyed out/marked inactive. A tooltip on hover displays:

"Timeline Conflict: This Strategy's dates ([Strategy Start Date] - [Strategy End Date]) do not overlap with the Group's dates ([Group Start Date] - [Group End Date/Ongoing]). Association is not possible."
(Example: "Timeline Conflict: This Strategy's dates (Mar 1, 2024 - Mar 31, 2024) do not overlap with the Group's dates (Apr 15, 2024 - Ongoing). Association is not possible.")

Partial/Full Overlap: The Strategy is selectable via a checkbox.

Step 4: Review Overlap Warnings (Post-selection, If Applicable)

After selecting one or more compatible Strategies, before proceeding to mapping, if any selection involves partial overlap, a dedicated "Timeline Considerations" section appears, listing clear warnings for each case:

Warning Type 1: Group Starts Before Strategy

Text: "Group '[Group Name]' starts on [Group Start Date], which is before Strategy '[Strategy Name]' starts on [Strategy Start Date]. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data from [Strategy Start Date] onwards will be considered."
(Example: "Group 'Spring Sale Push' starts on Mar 1, 2024, which is before Strategy 'Q2 Lead Gen' starts on Apr 1, 2024. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data from Apr 1, 2024 onwards will be considered.")

Warning Type 2: Group Ends After Strategy (Strategy has End Date)

Text: "Group '[Group Name]' ends on [Group End Date], which is after Strategy '[Strategy Name]' ends on [Strategy End Date]. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data up to [Strategy End Date] will be considered."
(Example: "Group 'Evergreen Content' ends on Dec 31, 2024, which is after Strategy 'Q3 Awareness Blitz' ends on Sep 30, 2024. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data up to Sep 30, 2024 will be considered.")

Warning Type 3: Group is Ongoing but Strategy Ends

Text: "Group '[Group Name]' is ongoing, but Strategy '[Strategy Name]' ends on [Strategy End Date]. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data up to [Strategy End Date] will be considered."
(Example: "Group 'Always-On Retargeting' is ongoing, but Strategy 'Summer Promo' ends on Aug 31, 2024. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data up to Aug 31, 2024 will be considered.")

Warning Type 4: Strategy Contains Group (Group timeframe is within Strategy timeframe)

Text: "Group '[Group Name]' timeframe ([Group Start Date] - [Group End Date]) falls entirely within the Strategy '[Strategy Name]' timeframe ([Strategy Start Date] - [Strategy End Date]). All Group campaign data within its dates will be considered for KR progress related to this Strategy." (This is informational, less of a warning)

Warning Type 5: Group Contains Strategy (Strategy timeframe is within Group timeframe)

Text: "Strategy '[Strategy Name]' timeframe ([Strategy Start Date] - [Strategy End Date]) falls entirely within the Group '[Group Name]' timeframe ([Group Start Date] - [Group End Date/Ongoing]). For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data between [Strategy Start Date] and [Strategy End Date] will be considered."
(Example: "Strategy 'July Flash Sale' timeframe (Jul 15, 2024 - Jul 21, 2024) falls entirely within the Group 'Summer Campaigns' timeframe (Jun 1, 2024 - Aug 31, 2024). For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data between Jul 15, 2024 and Jul 21, 2024 will be considered.")

Step 5: Map Campaign Metrics to Key Results

(Same as previous version) Proceeds only if valid selections exist. Prompts user to map metrics for each KR of the selected Strategy/Strategies, pulling available metrics from the current Group's campaigns.

Step 6: Validation & Confirmation

(Same as previous version) Validate mapping completion. User confirms. System saves links and mappings.

Step 7: UI Update

(Same as previous version) Group page updated. Confirmation message.

Acceptance Criteria:

Objective Category: Group interface clearly displays "Objective Category"; Secondary Objective is absent. Tooltips are updated.

Top Metrics Clarification: Documentation or tooltips clearly state the indicative nature of Group Top Metrics and the requirement for explicit mapping for KR tracking.

Initiation: User can trigger the association workflow from the Group view/edit interface.

Filtering: Strategies list must be filtered by matching "Objective Category".

Timeline Validation:

Strategies with no timeline overlap must be unselectable with the specific tooltip text provided.

Association must be blocked if no selectable Strategies exist due to timeline conflicts.

The specific, detailed warning texts for partial overlaps must be displayed accurately for relevant cases after selection but before final confirmation.

Selection: User can select one or more compatible Strategies.

Metric Mapping: Mapping UI must be presented for all KRs of selected Strategies, showing available metrics from the current Group's campaigns. Mapping completion must be validated.

Data Storage: Group <-> Strategy links and KR <-> Group Campaign Metric mappings must be saved accurately.

UI Update: Group page must reflect saved associations.

