Title: Associate Strategy with Groups and Map Metrics (From Strategy View)

User Story:

As a Marketing Planner using Grower,
When viewing an existing Strategy, I want to associate it with one or more relevant Groups (filtered by matching Objective Category and timeline compatibility) and map the Strategy's Key Result metrics to the selected Groups' campaign data, reviewing any timeline overlap implications,
so that I can define which execution units contribute to the Strategy and enable accurate KR tracking based on specific mapped metrics.

Complete Logic & Workflow:

Pre-requisites:

User is viewing an existing Strategy with a defined "Objective Category", associated KRs, and defined Start/End Dates.

Relevant Groups exist with the same "Objective Category" and defined Start/End Dates (End Date can be ongoing).

User has appropriate permissions (e.g., Edit Strategy).

Step 1: Initiation

User is on the Strategy details page.

User clicks a dedicated UI element like "Associate Groups", "Manage Group Associations", or similar.

Step 2: Select Groups for Association

A modal or dedicated UI section appears.

UI Title: "Associate Strategy '[Strategy Name]' with Groups"

Displays a list of Groups filtered to show only those sharing the same Objective Category as the current Strategy.

Information shown per Group: Group Name, Group Start Date, Group End Date (or "Ongoing").

Timeline Validation (Pre-selection Check): For each Group listed:

No Overlap: The Group is greyed out/marked inactive. A tooltip on hover displays:

"Timeline Conflict: This Group's dates ([Group Start Date] - [Group End Date/Ongoing]) do not overlap with the Strategy's dates ([Strategy Start Date] - [Strategy End Date]). Association is not possible."
(Example: "Timeline Conflict: This Group's dates (Apr 15, 2024 - Ongoing) do not overlap with the Strategy's dates (Mar 1, 2024 - Mar 31, 2024). Association is not possible.")

Partial/Full Overlap: The Group is selectable via a checkbox.

Step 3: Review Overlap Warnings (Post-selection, If Applicable)

After selecting one or more compatible Groups, before proceeding to mapping, a dedicated "Timeline Considerations" section appears, listing clear warnings for each case (using the exact same wording as defined in User Story 1, just referencing "this Strategy" instead of Strategy Name where appropriate):

Warning Type 1: Group Starts Before Strategy

Text: "Group '[Group Name]' starts on [Group Start Date], which is before this Strategy starts on [Strategy Start Date]. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data from [Strategy Start Date] onwards will be considered."

Warning Type 2: Group Ends After Strategy (Strategy has End Date)

Text: "Group '[Group Name]' ends on [Group End Date], which is after this Strategy ends on [Strategy End Date]. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data up to [Strategy End Date] will be considered."

Warning Type 3: Group is Ongoing but Strategy Ends

Text: "Group '[Group Name]' is ongoing, but this Strategy ends on [Strategy End Date]. For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data up to [Strategy End Date] will be considered."

Warning Type 4: Strategy Contains Group (Group timeframe is within Strategy timeframe)

Text: "Group '[Group Name]' timeframe ([Group Start Date] - [Group End Date]) falls entirely within this Strategy's timeframe ([Strategy Start Date] - [Strategy End Date]). All Group campaign data within its dates will be considered for KR progress related to this Strategy." (Informational)

Warning Type 5: Group Contains Strategy (Strategy timeframe is within Group timeframe)

Text: "This Strategy's timeframe ([Strategy Start Date] - [Strategy End Date]) falls entirely within the Group '[Group Name]' timeframe ([Group Start Date] - [Group End Date/Ongoing]). For calculating KR progress related to this Strategy, only Group campaign data between [Strategy Start Date] and [Strategy End Date] will be considered."

Step 4: Map Campaign Metrics to Key Results

(Same as previous version) Proceeds only if valid selections exist. Prompts user to map metrics for each KR of the current Strategy, pulling available metrics from the campaigns within each selected Group (UI needs to handle selecting metrics from potentially multiple groups per KR).

Step 5: Validation & Confirmation

(Same as previous version) Validate mapping completion. User confirms. System saves links and mappings.

Step 6: UI Update

(Same as previous version) Strategy page updated in the "Associated Groups" section. Confirmation message.

Acceptance Criteria:

Initiation: User can trigger the association workflow from the Strategy view interface.

Filtering: Groups list must be filtered by matching "Objective Category".

Timeline Validation:

Groups with no timeline overlap must be unselectable with the specific tooltip text provided.

Association must be blocked if no selectable Groups exist due to timeline conflicts.

The specific, detailed warning texts for partial overlaps must be displayed accurately for relevant cases after selection but before final confirmation.

Selection: User can select one or more compatible Groups.

Metric Mapping: Mapping UI must be presented for all KRs of the current Strategy, allowing selection of available metrics from the campaigns of each selected Group. Mapping completion must be validated.

Data Storage: Strategy <-> Group links and KR <-> Group Campaign Metric mappings must be saved accurately.

UI Update: Strategy page must reflect saved associations.

