Objective

To streamline the process of creating Groups within a Campaign Group – enabling Marketing Managers to efficiently establish and configure new Campaign segments with customized settings and objectives.

As a Marketing Manager on the Grower platform, I want to create Groups within a Campaign Group, so that I can strategize my Campaigns with precision and align them closely with my marketing goals.

Requirements

The GROUP CREATION process is initiated by clicking on the “+ Create Group” button located within the Group Listing page. For the user to access the Group Listing page and trigger the Group creation process, they will need to perform the following sequence of actions:

Group Creation User Action Flow
Consider the following requirements regarding the general layout of the Groups Creation process:

The title of the page should be “Create New Group”.

A check-done-02 icon (
) should be displayed inline to and preceding the page title.

The breadcrumbs of the Groups Listing page should be: {Organization Name} > Campaign Groups > {Campaign Group Name} > New Group

The placeholder data should be filled with the actual Organization Name and Campaign Group Name. For example: HOVI > Campaign Group > Pellini > New Group

Campaign Groups and {Campaign Group Name} within the breadcrumb should be clickable:

Clicking on “Campaign Groups” should redirect the user to the Campaign Group Listing page.

Clicking on the “Campaign Group Name” should redirect the user to the Summary page of the Campaign Group that they are currently in.

Creating A Group

User Story: I expect a user-friendly and efficient process. This involves navigating to the specific Campaign Group and accessing an intuitive form to input essential details for the new Group, such as its name, start and end dates, objectives. Additionally, I want to be able to select relevant digital channel campaigns and buyer personas associated with the Campaign Group. The creation process should include clear steps and validation checks to ensure that each Group is set up with the right parameters and aligns with the overarching goals of the Campaign Group.

Clicking on the “+ Create Group” button within the Group Listing page should initiate a multi-step creation process. This process should be designed to systematically guide users through the necessary steps for setting up a Group effectively. Each step should focus on specific aspects of Group configuration, ensuring comprehensive customization and optimization.

The multi-step creation process should span across the following pages:

Group Information: Users input basic information about the Group.

Add Your Campaign Activities: Users view and select Campaigns linked to the Campaign Group.

Add Website Pages: Users select website pages from Google Analytics 4 to include in the Group.

By dividing the Group creation process into distinct steps, users will be able to focus on one aspect at a time, reducing complexity and minimizing errors.

Step 1: Group Information

General Layout:

The header of this section should be “Step 1: Group Information”.

A footer navigation section should be displayed at the bottom of the page.

Step Indicator: The footer should display Step 1 out of 3 – i.e. the current step out of the total number of steps, with a visual emphasis on the current step.

Required Indicator: A blue dot visual indicator should be displayed to denote required fields, accompanied by the text "Required".

Navigation Buttons: The footer should include two navigation buttons: GO BACK and NEXT.

Clicking on the "GO BACK" button should navigate to the Group Listing page within the Campaign Group the Group is in – meaning, the user should be redirected to the Group Listing page within the “Groups” tab (i.e. the “Associated Groups” page).

Clicking on the “NEXT” button should navigate to Step 2.

The "NEXT" button should be disabled until all mandatory fields are completed.

