Acceptance Criteria

There are no limitations to how many Groups can be created with a Campaign Group.

Users must include at least one Campaign in a Group for it to be created. A Group cannot be created without any associated Campaigns.

Users can create Groups with a Start Date from the past, but this date must be capped at one fiscal year starting from the date of the Campaign Group creation.

Users can set the End Date to be three fiscal years in the future max or set it as ongoing by leaving the field blank.

Users must provide a unique name for each Group within the Campaign Group.

Users can only select Campaigns from channels already associated with the Campaign Group. Campaigns from channels not linked to the Campaign Group will not appear in the selection table and cannot be chosen.

A Campaign can be associated with multiple Groups.

The system should automatically update the status of Campaigns within a Group, indicating active or inactive statuses.

When changes are made at the Campaign Group level (updating a success metric, buyer persona change, channel addition), the system must automatically update those details on the Group level to reflect these changes.

The system should ensure that any newly added Campaigns at the Campaign Group level are included in the updated list of available Campaigns for selection in the Group.

