Okay, let's consolidate the key decisions and workflows into a single, comprehensive user story document tailored for your engineering team. This combines the Strategy definition, Group definition, Association workflow, the refined KR Tracking Setup, edge case handling, and permissions.

User Story Document: Strategy-Group Association and KR Tracking

1. Title: Implement Strategy Definition, Group Definition, Association, and Granular KR Tracking

2. User Story:

As a Marketing Planner (or Manager),

I want to define strategic marketing initiatives (Strategies with Objectives, Categories, and measurable Key Results), create operational execution units (Groups with a specific focus and associated campaigns/pages), link relevant Groups to Strategies based on matching focus areas, and configure detailed tracking for each Key Result by mapping specific metrics from associated Groups,

so that I can ensure clear alignment between strategy and execution, accurately measure progress towards strategic goals based on real performance data, and manage this linkage effectively even when plans or structures change.

3. Scope & Context:

This document covers the creation and management of Strategy and Group entities.

It details the process for establishing a many-to-many (N:M) association between Strategies and Groups.

It defines the critical workflow for configuring Key Result (KR) tracking by mapping specific data sources (TrackableMetricSource) to individual KRs within the context of a Strategy-Group association.

It outlines the handling of various edge cases (edits, deletions) and permission requirements.

It assumes the existence of Campaign Groups (CGs) which may hold overall budget ceilings, and that Initiatives/Campaigns (within Groups) are the source of actual spend and performance metric data (fetched via APIs or manual input).

4. Key Concepts & Definitions:

Strategy: A plan to achieve a marketing goal. Contains:

Objective Name: User-defined specific goal statement (e.g., "Penetrate Saudi Market 2025").

Objective Category: A single selection from a standard list (e.g., "Market Expansion", "Lead Generation") classifying the strategy's primary focus. Used for filtering.

Key Results (KRs): Specific, measurable outcomes with targets and dates. Defined as either Target Sum/Count or Target Rate/Average. Each KR has a descriptive Metric Label.

Planned Budget: Validated against CG Budget ceiling during Strategy creation/edit.

Timeline: Start/End dates.

Group: An operational unit containing Campaigns/Pages. Contains:

Group Focus: A single selection from the same standard list as Objective Category, defining the Group's primary contribution area. Used for filtering.

Timeline: Start/End dates (End date optional/ongoing).

Contents: Associated Campaigns, Pages.

Association (GroupStrategyAssociation): Represents the N:M link between a Group and a Strategy. Requires matching Group Focus == Objective Category and timeline overlap. Has a status (e.g., ACTIVE, MISMATCHED_CATEGORY, INACTIVE_NO_OVERLAP).

KR Tracking Setup (MetricKRMapping): The configuration defining how a specific KR's progress is measured via data from associated Groups. This links a KR (within an Association) to specific TrackableMetricSource items.

Trackable Metric Source (TrackableMetricSource): Represents a specific, granular data point available for mapping. Examples:

Unified Metrics (scoped): e.g., "Total Clicks (All Relevant Channels)", "Clicks (Snapchat Ads Only)".

Specific Ad Conversion Actions: e.g., "Google Ads: Conv Action 'Lead Form' (Campaign 'X')". Fetched via API segmentation.

Specific Platform Native Events: e.g., "LinkedIn Ads: Lead Gen Form 'Demo Request'".

Specific GA4 Goals/Events: e.g., "GA4: Goal 'Website Purchase'".

Manual Inputs: e.g., "Manual: Trade Show Leads".

Unified Metrics: Pre-defined, system-calculated aggregate metrics (Clicks, Impressions, Reach, CTR, CPC, CPA, ROAS) available for quick selection. Assumption: System knows how to calculate these based on the relevant context (all associated channels or specific selected channels). Need clarity on default conversions used for CPA/ROAS.

5. Core Workflows & Requirements:

5.1. Strategy Definition (Including Objective & KRs)

Trigger: User initiates Strategy creation.

Fields:

Objective Category (Mandatory): Single-select dropdown (Standard List).

Objective Name (Mandatory): Text input for specific goal statement.

Planned Budget (Mandatory): Currency input.

Timeline (Mandatory): Start/End Dates.

Other fields (Description, Type, Channels, Audience - as previously defined).

Budget Validation: Planned Budget MUST be validated against available CG Budget ceiling for the Strategy's timeline, considering other strategies' budgets (Implement detailed Scenarios 1-8 for validation logic). Provide actionable error/warning messages and potentially a "Request Budget Increase" workflow (saving strategy as draft, triggering notification).

KR Definition:

Trigger AI suggestions based on Objective Category and Objective Name.

User selects/edits/adds KRs (min. 1 mandatory).

Each KR requires:

KR Title (Text).

KR Type (Select: 'Target Sum/Count' OR 'Target Rate/Average').

Metric Label (Text - Descriptive label for the KR's metric).

Target Value (Numeric, allows negative for decreases).

Achievement Date (Date picker, future dates only, max 3 years out).

The "Metric Label" here is descriptive; actual data mapping happens later.

Outcome: Saved Strategy entity with associated Category, KRs, validated budget, etc.

5.2. Group Definition

Trigger: User initiates Group creation.

Fields:

Group Name (Mandatory, unique within CG).

Timeline (Mandatory Start Date, Optional/Ongoing End Date).

Group Focus (Mandatory): Single-select dropdown (Standard List - same as Objective Category). Essential for later association.

Other fields (Theme, Location, Personas - as previously defined).

Association Steps:

Step 2: Associate Campaigns (Handling timeline overlaps, status).

Step 3: Associate Website Pages (Via GA4 if connected).

Outcome: Saved Group entity with defined Focus, timeline, contents. No Objective/KR definition here.

5.3. Association Workflow (Linking Group <-> Strategy)

Trigger: User clicks "Associate Strategies" from Group view, or "Associate Groups" from Strategy view.

Filtering: System displays a list of potential Strategies/Groups filtered by:

Matching Categories: Group.Group Focus must == Strategy.Objective Category.

Timeline Overlap: There must be some overlap between the Group's and Strategy's active dates. Non-overlapping entities are greyed out/unselectable with clear tooltips explaining why.

Selection: User selects one or more compatible entities to associate.

Overlap Warnings: Display specific, non-blocking warnings detailing the nature of any partial timeline overlaps (as defined in original association stories).

Initiate KR Tracking Setup: Upon confirming the selection of associations, the user proceeds immediately to configure tracking for the KRs of the associated Strategy/Strategies in the context of the selected Group(s).

Outcome: Creates GroupStrategyAssociation record(s) with status = 'ACTIVE' (initially, or maybe NEEDS_MAPPING until tracking is set up).

5.4. KR Tracking Setup (Within Association Workflow Context)

Context: This UI appears after an association is created/edited, iterated for each KR belonging to the Strategy involved in the association.

UI Per KR: "Configure Tracking for KR: [KR Title] (Metric: [KR Metric Label])"

Guided Selection:

Offer Unified Metrics: Checkboxes for Unified Metrics (Clicks, Impressions, CTR, CPA, ROAS, etc.).

Requires clarifying how CPA/ROAS handle default conversions.

If selected, allow scoping: Radio buttons All Relevant Channels | Specific Channels (show channel checkboxes if specific).

Offer Specific Tracking: Button/Link "Track Specific Goals/Events". Clicking reveals:

A unified, searchable, filterable list of TrackableMetricSource items relevant to the associated Group's campaigns/channels (Specific Ad Actions segmented via API, GA4 Goals/Events, previously defined Manual Metrics, placeholder for new Manual Metric).

Handling KR Types:

If KR Type = 'Target Sum/Count': User selects one or more items from either the Unified list (Step 1) OR the Specific list (Step 2). System will SUM selected sources. Display Double-Counting Warning prominently if user selects potentially overlapping website conversion metrics from both GA4 and Ad Platforms within the Specific list. Guide user to choose ONE source of truth per event type.

If KR Type = 'Target Rate/Average':

Guide user to map components. E.g., For CPA: Map Cost Sources (Unified Cost OR specific costs from list), Map Conversion Sources (Unified default OR specific goals/actions from list).

System performs calculation: SUM(Costs) / SUM(Conversions).

Double-counting warnings apply within each component mapping.

Manual Metric Definition: If user selects the "Define New Manual Metric Input" placeholder, prompt for a name, save it, and allow selection. Actual data entry happens elsewhere.

State Storage: Save the selected TrackableMetricSource IDs against the specific KR within the context of the GroupStrategyAssociation.

Outcome: MetricKRMapping records created, linking Association+KR+MetricSource. Association status might become fully ACTIVE if previously NEEDS_MAPPING.

6. Handling Edits & Edge Cases (System Logic & UI Feedback):

Changing Group Focus / Objective Category:

Allow edit.

On save, check associated entities. If mismatch occurs:

Set GroupStrategyAssociation.status = 'MISMATCHED_CATEGORY'.

Pause KR contribution calculation from this association.

Display warning in UI.

Require user resolution (Revert, Align other entity, or Remove Association) via users with appropriate permissions.

Deleting Group/Strategy:

Warn user about breaking links.

On confirm, use cascade delete for GroupStrategyAssociation and MetricKRMapping records.

Changing Timelines:

If overlap reduces: KR calculations automatically adapt to new overlap period.

If no overlap: Set GroupStrategyAssociation.status = 'INACTIVE_NO_OVERLAP'. Pause KR contribution. Require user resolution.

Editing Strategy KRs:

KR Added: Flag association NEEDS_MAPPING_UPDATE. Prompt user later.

KR Deleted: Auto-delete linked MetricKRMapping records.

KR Edited (Target/Date): No action needed.

KR Edited (Meaning/Label): Flag association NEEDS_MAPPING_REVIEW.

Adding/Removing Campaigns in Group (Assuming some channel-level mapping):

Campaign Added: Data automatically included for relevant channel-level unified metrics. User may need to manually map specific conversion actions from the new campaign if desired.

Campaign Removed: Data automatically excluded for channel-level metrics. If a specific mapped conversion action was solely tied to the removed campaign, flag mapping as INVALID_MAPPING / NEEDS_REVIEW.

Source Metric Changes (e.g., Google Ads Action deleted):

Detect on data fetch failure.

Flag mapping BROKEN_SOURCE / INVALID_MAPPING. Notify user.

Disconnected Accounts:

Retain historical data.

Invalidate mappings linked to the disconnected source.

Flag associations NEEDS_RECONFIGURATION. Notify user.

7. Permissions:

Implement granular permissions (CRUD for Strategy, Group; specific permissions for managing associations & KR mapping).

Check permissions before allowing edits, deletions, association management, mapping configuration, and mismatch resolution actions.

Ensure system actions (like flagging mismatches, cascade deletes) occur even if the initiating user lacks full cross-entity permissions. Notifications may need to go to users with the required permissions to resolve issues flagged by others.

8. Backend Considerations:

Database schema to support all entities, relationships, statuses (Association Status, Mapping Status).

Robust API integrations for fetching granular, segmented Ad Platform data and GA4 data.

Validation Service for budget checks and association integrity checks on edits.

KR Calculation Engine respecting statuses, timelines, and mapping configurations (SUM for counts, Component calculation for rates).

Notification system/Task queue for user alerts and required actions.

RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) implementation.

9. Acceptance Criteria (High-Level Summary):

Users can create Strategies with Objectives, Categories, KRs, and validated Budgets.

Users can create Groups with a defined Group Focus and associated Campaigns/Pages.

Users can associate Groups and Strategies only if Categories match and timelines overlap.

Users can configure KR tracking by selecting appropriate Unified Metrics (scoped) OR specific granular metrics (Ad Actions, GA4 Goals, Manual).

System provides clear guidance and warnings regarding potential double-counting when selecting specific website conversion metrics from multiple sources (GA4+Ads).

System correctly handles Rate/Average KRs by allowing component mapping.

KR progress calculations accurately reflect the configured mappings, statuses, and timelines.

System correctly handles edge cases (category/timeline changes, KR edits, Group membership changes, deletions, disconnections) by updating statuses, pausing tracking where necessary, and prompting user resolution.

All actions are governed by a defined permission model.

