(English Translation for the Engineering Team)

1. Title: Implement OKR-Aligned Strategic Goals, Strategies, KPIs, Group Association, and Tracking

2. User Story:

As a Marketing Leader (e.g., CMO) or Planner,

I want to define high-level Strategic Objectives with measurable Key Results (KRs), create specific Strategies (Initiatives) linked to these objectives and KRs, define operational Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) for each Strategy, create Groups as execution units, link relevant Groups to Strategies, and configure detailed tracking for Strategy KPIs by mapping specific metrics from associated Groups,

so that I can establish a clear OKR structure, ensure alignment from top-level business goals down to tactical execution, accurately measure the performance of individual strategies via their KPIs, and monitor overall progress towards high-level Strategic Objectives and their Key Results.

3. Scope & Context:

This document outlines a hierarchical model: Strategic Objective -> Key Result (Objective Level) -> Strategy/Initiative -> KPI (Strategy Level) -> Group.

It covers the creation and management of Strategic Objective, Strategy, and Group entities.

It details the process for associating Strategies with Strategic Objectives and KRs.

It details the N:M association between Strategies and Groups.

It defines the workflow for configuring KPI tracking by mapping specific data sources (TrackableMetricSource) to individual Strategy KPIs.

It describes the necessary reporting views, including a "Strategic Objectives Dashboard" for high-level oversight.

It outlines handling for edge cases and permissions.

4. Key Concepts & Definitions:

Strategic Objective (The "O"): The high-level business goal (WHAT).

Attributes: Name, Description, Owner, Timeframe.

Contains: One or more high-level Key Results.

Key Result (KR - Objective Level): Measures the success of the parent Strategic Objective.

Attributes: KR Title/Description, Target (can be qualitative or quantitative), Owner, Timeframe.

Measurement: Progress is typically inferred from the success of contributing Strategy KPIs, potentially combined with manual updates or data from other systems (e.g., financial). Direct mapping from Group operational data is less common/often impossible for these high-level KRs.

Strategy / Initiative (The "How"): A specific plan/project to contribute towards one or more KRs of a parent Strategic Objective.

Attributes: Strategy Name / Initiative Title, Link to parent Strategic Objective, (Optional) Links to specific parent Key Results it influences, Objective Category (for classification/grouping/linking), Planned Budget, Timeline.

Contains: One or more specific KPIs.

KPI (Key Performance Indicator - Strategy Level): Measures the operational success of the Strategy itself.

Attributes: KPI Title, Type (Sum/Count or Rate/Average), Metric Label (descriptive), Target Value (numeric), Achievement Date.

Measurement: Directly measured by mapping TrackableMetricSource items from associated Groups.

Group: Operational execution unit containing Campaigns/Pages.

Attributes: Group Name, Group Focus (Category matching Strategy's Objective Category), Timeline, Contents.

Link: N:M with Strategy based on matching Group Focus == Strategy.Objective Category.

TrackableMetricSource: Granular data points available for KPI mapping (Unified Metrics scoped to channels, specific Ad Conversion Actions, specific GA4 Goals/Events, Manual Inputs).

Objective Category / Group Focus: Standard list of terms (e.g., "Brand Awareness", "Lead Generation") used for classifying Strategies and Groups to enable logical filtering during association.

5. Core Workflows & Requirements:

5.1. Strategic Objective & KR Definition (New Management Area)

Trigger: User navigates to a dedicated "Strategic Objectives" management section/page.

Functionality:

List existing Strategic Objectives.

"Create Strategic Objective" Button:

Form: Input Name, Description, Owner, Timeframe.

Add Key Results: Input KR Title, Target Description (e.g., "Reach 25% Market Share"). How progress is updated (e.g., Manual, % of Linked Strategy KPI completion - needs careful design) needs definition.

Edit/View existing Objectives and KRs.

Outcome: Defined Strategic Objective entities with their high-level Key Results.

5.2. Strategy Definition (Including KPIs)

Trigger: User initiates Strategy creation (likely from the Strategic Objectives view or a general Strategy list).

Fields:

Link to Parent Strategic Objective (Mandatory): Select from existing Strategic Objectives.

(Optional) Link to Parent Key Results: Multi-select which KRs of the parent Objective this Strategy primarily supports.

Strategy Name / Initiative Title (Mandatory): Text input.

Objective Category (Mandatory): Single-select dropdown (Standard List).

Planned Budget, Timeline, Other fields...

Budget Validation: Against CG Budget (if applicable).

KPI Definition:

Trigger AI suggestions based on Parent Objective, Strategy Name, Category.

User selects/edits/adds KPIs (min. 1 mandatory).

Each KPI requires: KPI Title, KPI Type (Sum/Count or Rate/Average), Metric Label, Target Value, Achievement Date.

Outcome: Saved Strategy entity, linked to a Strategic Objective, containing its own measurable KPIs.

5.3. Group Definition

(Essentially unchanged from previous descriptions): Focus on Group Name, Timeline, mandatory Group Focus (Category), associating Campaigns/Pages.

5.4. Association Workflow (Linking Group <-> Strategy)

(Essentially unchanged): Triggered from Group or Strategy. Filter list based on matching Group.Group Focus == Strategy.Objective Category and timeline overlap. Select entities, review overlap warnings. Proceed to KPI Tracking Setup.

5.5. KPI Tracking Setup (Within Association Context)

(Essentially unchanged, but using "KPI" terminology): Iterate through the Strategy's KPIs.

Guided UI:

Offer Unified Metrics (scoped).

Offer access to Specific Metrics list (TrackableMetricSource items relevant to associated Group's context).

Adapt UI for KPI Type: Sum/Count (select sources, system SUMS, watch for double-count warnings on website conversions) vs. Rate/Average (map components, system calculates rate, warnings apply within components).

Allow defining/selecting Manual inputs.

Outcome: Saved MetricKPIMapping records linking Association+KPI+MetricSource.

6. Strategic Objectives Dashboard (CMO View)

Purpose: Provide high-level overview of progress towards business goals.

Structure: Organized by Strategic Objective.

Content per Objective:

Display Objective Name & High-Level KRs.

Show KR status/progress (based on linked Strategy KPI progress or manual updates - calculation needs careful definition).

List linked Strategies.

Show summary status/progress for each linked Strategy (based on its KPI completion, budget pacing).

Potentially show rolled-up budget vs. spend for all Strategies under the Objective.

Allow drill-down to Strategy details.

7. Handling Edits & Edge Cases:

(Largely unchanged from previous descriptions, applying to the new structure):

Changing Group Focus / Strategy.Objective Category: Allow edit, flag association mismatch, pause KPI contribution, require resolution.

Deleting Entities: Use cascade deletes for associations/mappings, warn user.

Changing Timelines: Adjust calculation periods or flag if no overlap.

Editing Strategy KPIs: Flag association (NEEDS_MAPPING_UPDATE / NEEDS_MAPPING_REVIEW), delete mappings for deleted KPIs.

Group Membership Changes: Auto-include/exclude for channel-level Unified Metrics. Flag if specific mapped conversion action source is removed.

Source Metric Changes / Disconnected Accounts: Detect failure, flag mappings (BROKEN_SOURCE), notify user for reconfiguration. Retain history.

8. Permissions:

Need CRUD permissions for Strategic Objectives & their KRs.

Need CRUD permissions for Strategies & their KPIs.

Need CRUD permissions for Groups.

Need specific permissions for managing associations (MANAGE_STRATEGY_ASSOCIATIONS, MANAGE_GROUP_ASSOCIATIONS) which include KPI mapping configuration.

Ensure permissions are checked for all edits, deletions, linking, mapping, and resolution workflows.

9. Backend Considerations:

Database schema for Strategic Objectives, Key Results (Objective Level), Strategies, KPIs (Strategy Level), linking tables, Groups, TrackableMetricSources, GroupStrategyAssociations (with status), MetricKPIMappings (with status).

Logic for calculating high-level KR progress (potentially complex).

Robust KPI Calculation Engine respecting statuses, timelines, mapping, KPI types.

Other dependencies remain (Validation, APIs, Notifications, RBAC).

