This document replaces previous versions and outlines the complete structure and core workflows.

Consolidated User Story: OKR-Aligned Strategic Planning, Execution Linking, and Performance Tracking

1. Introduction & Goal

Overall User Need: As a Marketing Leader or Planner using Grower, I need a clear, structured system to define high-level business goals (Strategic Objectives with Key Results), create specific Strategies (Initiatives) aimed at achieving them, define measurable operational KPIs for each Strategy, manage execution units (Groups), link Groups to Strategies effectively, and track KPI progress based on actual performance data, ultimately providing visibility into both strategic initiative performance and overall progress towards business objectives.

Purpose of this Document: To provide engineering with the definitive requirements for the data model, core workflows, tracking mechanisms, reporting needs, edge case handling, and permissions for this OKR-aligned planning and execution framework.

2. Scope & Context:

Defines the hierarchical model: Strategic Objective -> Key Result (KR) -> Strategy/Initiative -> Key Performance Indicator (KPI) -> Group.

Covers CRUD operations for Strategic Objective, Strategy, and Group entities.

Details the linking process: Strategy to Strategic Objective/KR, and Group (N:M) to Strategy.

Defines the workflow for configuring KPI tracking by mapping TrackableMetricSource items.

Outlines requirements for a Strategic Objectives Dashboard and handling of common edge cases and permissions.

Assumes Campaign Groups (CGs) may provide budget context and that Groups contain Campaigns/Pages sourcing performance data.

3. Defined Hierarchy:

Strategic Objective (Top - The "O"): The high-level business goal (WHAT).

Key Result (KR - Objective Level): Measures the success of the parent Strategic Objective. Progress often inferred or manually updated.

Strategy / Initiative (Mid - The "How"): A specific plan linked to a Strategic Objective (and optionally specific KRs) containing its own measurable targets.

KPI (Key Performance Indicator - Strategy Level): Measures the operational success of the Strategy itself. Directly tracked via Group data.

Group (Execution): Operational unit linked N:M to Strategies, executing campaigns and providing data for KPIs.

4. Key Concepts & Definitions:

Strategic Objective: High-level goal. Attributes: Name, Description, Owner, Timeframe. Contains KRs.

Key Result (KR): Objective-level success measure. Attributes: Title/Description, Target (qualitative/quantitative), Owner, Timeframe. Measurement logic needs careful design (often indirect).

Strategy / Initiative: Specific plan. Attributes: Strategy Name, Link to parent Strategic Objective, (Optional) Links to parent KRs, Objective Category (classification), Planned Budget, Timeline. Contains KPIs.

KPI: Strategy-level success measure. Attributes: KPI Title, KPI Type (Sum/Count or Rate/Average), Metric Label, Target Value, Achievement Date. Directly Measured via mapping.

Group: Execution unit. Attributes: Group Name, Group Focus (Category), Timeline, Contents (Campaigns/Pages).

TrackableMetricSource: Granular data point for KPI mapping. Includes: Unified Metrics (scoped), specific Ad Conversion Actions (via API), specific Platform Native Events (e.g., LinkedIn Lead Forms), specific GA4 Goals/Events, Manual Inputs. Must clearly identify source and conceptual outcome.

Objective Category / Group Focus: Standard list (e.g., "Brand Awareness", "Lead Generation") used on Strategies and Groups respectively for classification and filtering during association (Group Focus must match Strategy.Objective Category).

GroupStrategyAssociation: Record representing the N:M link between a Group and Strategy, requires matching category/focus and timeline overlap. Has a status (e.g., ACTIVE, MISMATCHED_CATEGORY).

MetricKPIMapping: Record linking an Association + KPI + TrackableMetricSource. Defines how a specific KPI is tracked. Has a status (e.g., ACTIVE, BROKEN_SOURCE).

5. Core Workflows & Requirements:

(5.1) Strategic Objective & KR Definition (Dedicated Management Area)

UI: A distinct section/page for managing Strategic Objectives.

Functionality: List, Create, Edit, View Objectives.

Creation Flow:

Define Objective: Name, Description, Owner, Timeframe.

Define associated KRs: KR Title, Target Description. Define how KR progress will be updated (e.g., Manual entry placeholder, Roll-up from linked Strategy KPIs - specify calculation logic, Integration placeholder).

Outcome: Creates Strategic Objective and associated Key Result records.

(5.2) Strategy Definition (Including KPIs)

UI: Strategy creation/edit form.

Fields & Flow:

Link to Parent Strategic Objective (Mandatory): Select from list created in 5.1.

(Optional) Link to Parent KRs: Multi-select specific KRs this Strategy supports.

Strategy Name / Initiative Title (Mandatory Text).

Objective Category (Mandatory Dropdown - Standard List).

Planned Budget, Timeline, Audience, Channels etc.

Budget Validation: Against CG ceiling (implement Scenarios 1-8 logic).

KPI Definition:

AI suggests relevant KPIs based on parent Objective, Strategy Name, Category.

User selects/edits/adds KPIs (min. 1).

Each KPI requires: KPI Title, KPI Type (Sum/Count or Rate/Average), Metric Label, Target Value, Achievement Date.

Outcome: Saved Strategy entity, linked upwards, containing its own KPIs ready for tracking configuration.

(5.3) Group Definition

UI: Group creation/edit wizard.

Fields & Flow: Group Name, Timeline, Group Focus (Mandatory Dropdown - Standard List), Theme, Location, Personas. Associate Campaigns & Pages.

Outcome: Saved Group entity classified by its Group Focus.

(5.4) Association Workflow (Linking Group <-> Strategy)

UI: Triggered from Group or Strategy details page ("Manage Associations").

Logic:

Display list of potential Groups/Strategies filtered strictly by Group.Group Focus == Strategy.Objective Category AND Timeline Overlap.

Disable selection for non-matching/non-overlapping items with clear tooltips.

User selects one or more valid entities.

Display non-blocking warnings for partial timeline overlaps.

On confirmation, create GroupStrategyAssociation record(s) and proceed immediately to KPI Tracking Setup for the new association(s).

Outcome: Establishes the link, ready for tracking setup.

(5.5) KPI Tracking Setup (Within Association Context)

UI: Presented per-KPI after an association is made/edited. Title: "Configure Tracking for KPI: [KPI Title] (Metric: [KPI Metric Label])".

Guided Flow:

Offer Unified Metrics: Checkboxes for standard metrics (Clicks, Impressions, etc.) scoped to the relevant channels from the associated Group(s). Allow scoping choice: All Relevant Channels | Specific Channels.

Offer Specific Metrics: Button/Section "Track Specific Goals/Events". Reveals filterable/searchable list of TrackableMetricSource items (Specific Ad Actions, GA4 Goals, Manual etc.) relevant to the associated Group(s).

Logic Based on KPI Type:

Sum/Count: User selects ONE OR MORE sources from Unified list OR Specific list. System SUMS values. Display prominent Double-Counting Warning if potential duplicates (e.g., website conversions from GA4 + Ad Platform) are selected from the Specific list. User must choose source of truth.

Rate/Average: Guide user to map required components (e.g., Cost sources, Conversion sources). User selects specific TrackableMetricSource items for each component. System calculates the rate SUM(Numerator Components) / SUM(Denominator Components). Double-counting warnings apply within component selection.

Manual Metrics: Allow defining new manual metric names via placeholder selection.

Outcome: Saved MetricKPIMapping records detailing how each KPI is measured for that specific association.

6. Reporting & Dashboards

Strategic Objectives Dashboard (CMO View):

Organized by Strategic Objective.

Shows high-level KR status/progress (calculation TBD - based on Strategy KPI progress / manual updates).

Lists linked Strategies with their summary status (based on their KPI progress & budget pacing).

Provides roll-up views (e.g., budget).

Allows drill-down to Strategy details.

Strategy Details Page: Shows Strategy info, lists its KPIs with detailed progress (calculated from mappings), budget vs. actual, lists associated Groups.

Group Details Page: Shows Group info, lists associated Strategies.

7. Handling Edits & Edge Cases

Implement robust handling for changes post-association:

Group Focus/Objective Category mismatch -> Flag association, pause KPI contribution, require resolution.

Entity Deletion -> Cascade delete associations/mappings, warn user.

Timeline Changes -> Adjust calculation periods or flag if no overlap.

KPI Edits -> Flag association for mapping update/review, handle deletions cleanly.

Group Membership Changes -> Auto-adjust channel-level metrics; flag mappings if specific source campaign removed.

Source Metric Changes/Disconnections -> Detect failure, flag mappings, notify user. Retain history.

8. Permissions

Implement distinct CRUD permissions for Strategic Objectives (+KRs), Strategies (+KPIs), Groups.

Implement specific permissions for managing associations and configuring KPI tracking (MANAGE_STRATEGY_ASSOCIATIONS, MANAGE_GROUP_ASSOCIATIONS).

Enforce checks consistently across all relevant actions and resolution workflows.

9. Backend Considerations

Schema supporting all entities, links, statuses.

Logic for high-level KR progress calculation/update.

KPI Calculation Engine (respecting statuses, timelines, mapping, types).

API Integrations (granular, segmented data fetching).

Validation Service (budget, associations).

Notification System.

RBAC Implementation.

