so that I can establish the top-level goals and success criteria that subsequent marketing Strategies will align with and contribute towards.

3. Scope & Context:

This workflow occurs within a dedicated "Strategic Objectives Management" section of the application.

It focuses solely on creating the top-level Strategic Objective entity and its direct Key Results.

This is distinct from, and typically precedes, the creation of individual Strategy entities (which will later link to these Strategic Objectives and KRs).

4. Complete Logic & Workflow:

(Step 1: Define Strategic Objective)

User initiates the creation of a new Strategic Objective (e.g., clicks "Create Strategic Objective").

UI Fields:

Strategic Objective Name (Mandatory Text Input):

Placeholder: e.g., "Enter the high-level business objective like 'Increase EU Market Share'"

Tooltip: "Define the primary, overarching business goal this objective represents."

Description (Optional Text Area):

Placeholder: "Provide more context about this strategic objective..."

Owner (Optional - User Selection/Input): Identify the primary owner or responsible party.

Timeframe (Optional Date Range or Period Selection - e.g., FY2025, Q4 2024): Define the period this objective is relevant for.

Validation: Strategic Objective Name is mandatory.

(Step 2: Define Key Results (KRs) - Objective Level)

After defining the objective details, the user proceeds to define its Key Results.

AI Assistance (Optional Trigger):

User can optionally click "Suggest Key Results" or similar.

AI uses the Strategic Objective Name and Description as context.

AI suggests 3-5 high-level, ambitious Key Results appropriate for measuring the overall objective. (See updated AI Prompt below).

UI for Defining KRs:

Users can select/edit AI suggestions or add KRs manually.

A minimum of one KR is recommended but might not be strictly mandatory initially (TBD).

Fields per KR:

KR Title / Description (Mandatory Text Input): Clearly state the Key Result. (e.g., "Reach 25% Market Share in Germany", "Increase new customer acquisition in France by 40%", "Successfully launch Brand Refresh campaign").

Target Description (Optional Text Input): Elaborate on the target or success criteria if needed (especially for qualitative KRs). The specific numeric target might live here or be part of the Title.

Owner (Optional - User Selection/Input): Owner for this specific KR.

Achievement Date / Target Date (Mandatory Date Picker): By when should this KR be achieved? (Validation: Future date, max 3 years out).

Progress Update Method (Recommended - Dropdown/Radio): How will progress typically be tracked?

Options: "Manual Update", "Roll-up from Linked Strategy KPIs" (requires later configuration), "Integration (Specify)". Sets expectation but doesn't configure tracking here.

Key Distinction: Note the absence of a directly mappable "Metric Label" or strictly enforced "Target Numeric Value" like in Strategy KPIs. KRs at this level can be more strategic or qualitative, and their measurement is often indirect.

(Step 3: Review and Save)

User reviews the Strategic Objective details and the list of defined Key Results.

User confirms submission via a "Save Strategic Objective" button.

