When: Triggered optionally when the user is defining KRs for a new Strategic Objective.

Data: Strategic Objective Name, Strategic Objective Description.

Prompt:

You are an AI strategic planning assistant. Based on the provided high-level Strategic Objective, suggest 3-5 ambitious and measurable Key Results (KRs) that define success for this objective. These KRs should focus on outcomes and impact.

Each suggested Key Result must include:

KR Title/Description: A clear statement of the result to be achieved (e.g., "Increase Market Share in X Region", "Improve Customer Satisfaction Score", "Launch Y Successfully").

Target Description: A brief elaboration on the target (e.g., "to 25%", "by 15 points", "with positive media coverage").

Recommended Achievement Date: A realistic target date.

Provided Context:
Strategic Objective Name: {User Entered Name}
Strategic Objective Description: {User Entered Description}

Focus on suggesting KRs that reflect genuine business outcomes relevant to the Objective. Avoid overly operational metrics unless they directly represent the Objective's success. Format clearly.

6. Acceptance Criteria (Updated):

Users can access a dedicated area to manage Strategic Objectives.

Users must provide a Name when creating a Strategic Objective.

Users can define one or more Key Results (KRs) associated with a Strategic Objective.

Each KR requires at least a Title/Description and an Achievement Date.

AI can optionally suggest relevant high-level KRs based on the Objective's definition.

Users can edit KR details (Title, Target Description, Date).

The system saves the Strategic Objective and its associated KRs correctly.

This workflow is separate from the Strategy creation workflow.

Validation ensures Achievement Date is logical (future, within limits).

