Updated User Story: Validate Strategy Planned Budget Against Campaign Group Budget

1. Title: Validate Strategy Planned Budget Against Campaign Group Budget Ceiling

2. User Story:

As a Marketing Planner defining or editing a Strategy,

I want the system to automatically validate the Planned Budget I enter for the Strategy against the available budget ceiling defined in the parent Campaign Group (CG), considering the CG's budget recurrence (monthly, quarterly, yearly), the planned budgets of other existing Strategies within the same CG, and handling periods with undefined CG budgets,

so that I can ensure my strategic plans are financially feasible within the overall constraints, receive clear feedback if adjustments are needed, and have options to address budget conflicts without being completely blocked.

3. Scope & Context:

This validation occurs during the Strategy creation and editing workflow, specifically when the Planned Budget field is populated or modified.

It compares the Strategy.Planned Budget against the available portion of the CG Budget Ceiling for the Strategy.Timeline.

It assumes CG Budgets can be set monthly, quarterly, or yearly, or be undefined.

It requires calculating the available budget by accounting for other strategies sharing the same CG budget pool during overlapping time periods.

4. Core Concept: Calculating Available CG Budget for a Strategy Timeline

(This section remains unchanged from the previous version, emphasizing precision in pro-rating and subtracting other strategies' planned budgets period-by-period)

Identify Relevant CG Budget Periods: Determine all CG budget periods (months, quarters, years) overlapping the Strategy's timeline.

Calculate Pro-Rated CG Budget for Strategy Timeline: For each overlapping CG period, calculate the portion of the total CG budget ceiling applicable to the specific days the Strategy runs within that period (ideally using actual days per period).

Account for Other Strategies: Subtract the Planned Budgets of all other existing Strategies within the same CG active during the same overlapping periods (perform subtraction period-by-period before summing).

Result = Available CG Budget: The maximum budget ceiling available from the CG for the specific Strategy being evaluated.

5. Requirements & Scenarios:

(Scenarios 1, 4, 6, 7, 8 remain logically the same, focusing on the calculation and comparison. Key updates are in Scenario 2, 3, 5 and the general error handling based on our previous discussion)

