(Logic unchanged) Before saving CG changes (amount or recurrence), re-validate ALL associated Strategies against the proposed new CG budget structure.

Handling:

If all Strategies remain valid -> Allow saving CG changes.

If any Strategy becomes invalid -> Block saving CG changes. Display error identifying conflicting Strategies and requiring adjustment of those Strategy budgets before the CG budget change can be saved.

6. Acceptance Criteria (Updated Terminology & Handling)

System correctly calculates Available CG Budget for a Strategy's timeline, considering CG recurrence, pro-rating, and Planned Budgets of other concurrent Strategies.

Strategy Planned Budget is validated against Available CG Budget during Strategy create/edit.

If budget exceeds limit, saving is blocked, a clear error message is shown indicating the limit, and actionable options (adjust budget/timeline, optionally request CG increase) are presented.

Undefined future CG budgets trigger warnings and use estimates (or $0) for validation; Strategies are flagged for review. Notifications are sent when budgets are defined.

Completely undefined CG budgets allow saving but trigger a strong warning.

Editing the CG Budget triggers re-validation of all associated Strategies, blocking the CG change if conflicts arise until Strategy budgets are adjusted.

All error messages and warnings are clear, specific, and actionable.

